    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="0539" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2245c</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chinese
                        Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Yung Kwai</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-31"><hi rendition="#italic">May 31,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Lansing’s Note No. 82 of
                    October 8, 1918,<anchor n="99" xml:id="d377-f1"/> on the subject of the
                    formation of an international group for the purpose of rendering financial
                    assistance to China, I have the honor to enclose herewith for your information
                    and for the information of your Government copy of an identic note with
                    accompanying enclosure on the above mentioned subject, which I have today handed
                    to the representatives of Great Britain, France and Japan.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d377-f2"/></p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Breckinridge Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
